# OpenAI API settings for the labs.
# Copy this file to .env and edit it. Never commit .env.
#
# 1. Create a key at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# 2. Paste it as OPENAI_API_KEY. The official SDK reads that name.
#    A real key looks like sk-... — do not commit one.
# 3. MODEL is optional. gpt-4.1-mini supports tool calling for
#    Chapters 2 and 3. See:
#    https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-4.1-mini
#
# Shell variables win over this file. Do not export a real API key
# into a shared shell history if you can keep it in .env instead.
# Leave this blank until you paste a key. An empty value exits
# before any request.

OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Blank uses gpt-4.1-mini. Chapter 3 changes only this
# line (for example gpt-4.1) and leaves the rest of the harness alone.
MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini
